INFO     rag_service.services.generation_service:generation_service.py:427 {"event": "rag_query_trace", "query": "What is the investigational medicinal product?", "retrieval_query": null, "system_prompt_version": "440b2406", "retrieved_chunks": [{"title": "Protocol Ulcerative Colitis", "page": 12, "section": "Investigational Medicinal Product (IMP)", "score": null, "scores": [0.9985506, 0.9985506, 0.9981324, 0.9981324], "had_context": true}, {"title": "Protocol Ulcerative Colitis", "page": 1, "section": "A Phase II, Randomized, Double-blind, Placebo-controlled Study to Evaluate the Safety and Efficacy of TJ301 (FE 999301) Administered Intravenously in Patients with Active Ulcerative Colitis", "score": null, "scores": [0.9856076, 0.9856076], "had_context": true}], "context_char_count": 5814, "response": "Source: Protocol Ulcerative Colitis.pdf\n\nThe investigational medicinal product (IMP) in this trial is as follows:\n\n1. **Name:** TJ301, also referred to as FE 999301 and Olamkicept (proposed INN).\n[Section A Phase II, Randomized, Double-blind, Placebo-controlled Study to Evaluate the Safety and Efficacy of TJ301 (FE 999301) Administered Intravenously in Patients with Active Ulcerative Colitis \u00b7 p.1]\n\n2. **Formulation:** 15 mg/mL solution for injection, composed of 25 mM histidine, 200 mM sucrose, and 0.1 mg/mL Polysorbate 20 in aqueous solution.\n[Section Investigational Medicinal Product (IMP) \u00b7 p.12]\n\n3. **Route of administration:** Intravenous infusion, diluted in 250 mL 5% (w/v) glucose, administered over 2 hours.\n[Section Investigational Medicinal Product (IMP) \u00b7 p.12]\n\n4. **Storage:** Both TJ301 and placebo should be stored at -20 \u00b1 5 \u00b0C and thawed at the site by site personnel (blind to study randomisation).\n[Section Investigational Medicinal Product (IMP) \u00b7 p.12]", "sources": [{"name": "Protocol Ulcerative Colitis", "page": 1, "section": "A Phase II, Randomized, Double-blind, Placebo-controlled Study to Evaluate the Safety and Efficacy of TJ301 (FE 999301) Administered Intravenously in Patients with Active Ulcerative Colitis", "exactText": "Investigational Medicinal Product: TJ301 (solution for injection), also referred to as FE 999301 and Olamkicept", "bboxes": [[72.0, 578.6639829101563, 168.0, 568.2525283647018]], "relevance": "high"}, {"name": "Protocol Ulcerative Colitis", "page": 12, "section": "Investigational Medicinal Product (IMP)", "exactText": "The IMP in this trial is TJ301 (FE 999301, Olamkicept (proposed INN)) (15 mg/mL in solution for injection [25 mM histidine, 200 mM sucrose, 0.1 mg/mL Polysorbate 20 in aqueous solution]). The placebo is the solution for injection [25 mM histidine, 200 mM sucrose, 0.1 mg/mL Polysorbate 20 in aqueous solution] without TJ301. Both placebo and TJ301 should be stored at -20 \u00b1 5 \u00b0C and thawed at the site by site personnel (blind to study randomisation) and diluted in 250 mL 5% (w/v) glucose. The infusion time is 2 hours.", "bboxes": [[72.0, 529.2239829101562, 552.2400000000001, 473.4549752178485], [68.52363586425781, 395.688720703125, 553.8070678710938, 261.00616455078125]], "relevance": "high"}], "timing": {"response_cache_hit": false, "semantic_cache_hit": false, "chunks_compressed": true, "condense_ms": 0.008541159331798553, "query_condensed": false, "embedding_ms": 685.7477077282965, "embedding_cache_hit": false, "retrieval": {"chunk_cache_hit": false, "confidence_filter_applied": true, "confidence_filter_threshold": 0.04, "confidence_filter_bm25_threshold": null, "confidence_filter_input_count": 52, "confidence_filter_kept_count": 52, "confidence_filter_dropped_count": 0, "confidence_filter_kept_scores": [0.5965, 0.5631, 0.5626, 0.5614, 0.5212, 0.5104, 0.4998, 0.4963, 0.4766, 0.4707, 0.4646, 0.4564, 0.4544, 0.4536, 0.4531, 0.4508, 0.4505, 0.4502, 0.4444, 0.4428, 0.441, 0.4402, 0.4392, 0.4382, 0.4355, 0.4345, 0.4331, 0.4325, 0.4311, 0.43, 0.4283, 0.4253, 0.425, 0.4236, 0.4205, 0.4189, 0.4178, 0.4176, 0.4159, 0.4158, 0.4