INFO     rag_service.services.generation_service:generation_service.py:427 {"event": "rag_query_trace", "query": "How is randomisation stratified in this study?", "retrieval_query": null, "system_prompt_version": "440b2406", "retrieved_chunks": [{"title": "Protocol Ulcerative Colitis", "page": 36, "section": "4.2.2 Randomisation", "score": 0.9896718, "scores": null, "had_context": true}, {"title": "Protocol Ulcerative Colitis", "page": 92, "section": "Appendix 4 - Summary of Changes for Version 1.1", "score": 0.9874721, "scores": null, "had_context": true}, {"title": "Protocol Ulcerative Colitis", "page": 26, "section": "3.1.2 Overall Design", "score": null, "scores": [0.961678, 0.961678], "had_context": true}, {"title": "Protocol Ulcerative Colitis", "page": 8, "section": "Study Design", "score": null, "scores": [0.84453726, 0.84453726], "had_context": true}], "context_char_count": 6452, "response": "Source: Protocol Ulcerative Colitis.pdf\n\nRandomisation in this study is stratified by two factors:\n\n1. **Prior corticosteroids treatment** (yes/no)\n[Section 4.2.2 Randomisation \u00b7 p.36]\n\n2. **Consent to participate in PK substudy** (yes/no)\n[Section 4.2.2 Randomisation \u00b7 p.36]\n\nThese two stratification factors replaced an earlier version of the protocol (Version 1.0), which had originally stratified by elevated CRP levels (\u22653 mg/L) and stable conventional treatment history. The stratification information is collected at Visit 1 and used at Visit 2 (the Randomisation Visit) when patients are allocated via a validated Interactive Web Response System (IWRS) in a 1:1:1 ratio to placebo, TJ301 300 mg, or TJ301 600 mg.\n[Section Appendix 4 - Summary of Changes for Version 1.1 \u00b7 p.92]", "sources": [{"name": "Protocol Ulcerative Colitis", "page": 36, "section": "4.2.2 Randomisation", "exactText": "Randomisation will be stratified by prior corticosteroids treatment (yes/no) and consent to participate in PK substudy (yes/no). This information will be collected at Visit 1 and will be used at Visit 2 for randomisation by stratification based on these factors.", "bboxes": [[72.0, 233.90398291015606, 538.44, 178.01497521784836]], "relevance": "high"}, {"name": "Protocol Ulcerative Colitis", "page": 26, "section": "3.1.2 Overall Design", "exactText": "Randomisation will be stratified by prior corticosteroids treatment (yes/no) and consent to participate in PK substudy (yes/no).", "bboxes": [[72.0, 603.5039829101565, 518.28, 593.2149752178489]], "relevance": "high"}, {"name": "Protocol Ulcerative Colitis", "page": 92, "section": "Appendix 4 - Summary of Changes for Version 1.1", "exactText": "90 patients will be centrally, dynamically, stratified randomly (by elevated ( \u22653 mg/L) CRP levels, and stable conventional treatment (prior treatment with amino salicylates, corticosteroids, and immunosuppressive drugs)) assigned to 3 groups (1:1:1)... Randomisation will be stratified by prior corticosteroids treatment (yes/no) and consent to participate in PK substudy (yes/no).", "bboxes": [[52.59044647216797, 495.76949310302734, 771.7723999023438, 121.96722412109375]], "relevance": "medium"}], "timing": {"response_cache_hit": false, "semantic_cache_hit": false, "chunks_compressed": true, "condense_ms": 0.0012498348951339722, "query_condensed": false, "embedding_ms": 884.1430838219821, "embedding_cache_hit": false, "retrieval": {"chunk_cache_hit": false, "confidence_filter_applied": true, "confidence_filter_threshold": 0.04, "confidence_filter_bm25_threshold": null, "confidence_filter_input_count": 47, "confidence_filter_kept_count": 47, "confidence_filter_dropped_count": 0, "confidence_filter_kept_scores": [0.634, 0.6292, 0.6291, 0.5958, 0.5617, 0.5299, 0.5258, 0.5183, 0.5032, 0.5019, 0.4899, 0.488, 0.488, 0.4846, 0.4815, 0.4781, 0.471, 0.4668, 0.4638, 0.4619, 0.4613, 0.4606, 0.459, 0.455, 0.4532, 0.4512, 0.4501, 0.4494, 0.4453, 0.4438, 0.4434, 0.4423, 0.4409, 0.4374, 0.4355, 0.4345, 0.4317, 0.4312, 0.4302, 0.4255, 0.424