INFO     rag_service.services.generation_service:generation_service.py:427 {"event": "rag_query_trace", "query": "What are the study periods and their durations?", "retrieval_query": null, "system_prompt_version": "440b2406", "retrieved_chunks": [{"title": "Protocol Ulcerative Colitis", "page": 9, "section": "Study Flowchart", "score": null, "scores": [0.39565945, 0.033844035, 0.03191915], "had_context": true}, {"title": "Protocol Ulcerative Colitis", "page": 43, "section": "6.1 Trial Flowchart", "score": 0.33155245, "scores": null, "had_context": true}, {"title": "Protocol Ulcerative Colitis", "page": 8, "section": "Study Flowchart", "score": 0.19713514, "scores": null, "had_context": true}, {"title": "Protocol Ulcerative Colitis", "page": 27, "section": "3.1.2 Overall Design", "score": 0.015967654, "scores": null, "had_context": true}], "context_char_count": 6089, "response": "Source: Protocol Ulcerative Colitis.pdf\n\nThe study consists of the following periods and their durations:\n\n1. **Run-in Period** (Visit 0): An optional period for patients who need to stabilise their conventional UC treatment before entering the Screening Period. Duration is variable, depending on how long it takes to meet the stability criteria (e.g., up to 6 months for AZA/6-MP stabilisation).\n[Section Study Flowchart \u00b7 p.8]\n\n2. **Screening Period** (Visit 1): A 4-week screening period (Days -28 to -1 prior to Visit 2), during which disease activity assessments including endoscopy are performed.\n[Section Study Flowchart \u00b7 p.9]\n\n3. **12-week double-blind Treatment Period** (Visits 2\u20138): Begins at the Randomisation Visit (Baseline) and includes 5 visits during the treatment period, concluding at the End of Treatment (EoT) Visit at Week 12.\n[Section 6.1 Trial Flowchart \u00b7 p.43]\n\n4. **Safety Follow-up Period** (Visit 9): A 3-week safety follow-up period, scheduled at 35 days after the last dose of IMP (Day 105 / Week 15) for patients completing the trial. For pat