INFO     rag_service.services.generation_service:generation_service.py:427 {"event": "rag_query_trace", "query": "What are the main exclusion criteria?", "retrieval_query": null, "system_prompt_version": "440b2406", "retrieved_chunks": [{"title": "Protocol Ulcerative Colitis", "page": 10, "section": "Exclusion Criteria", "score": 0.95998776, "scores": null, "had_context": true}, {"title": "Protocol Ulcerative Colitis", "page": 34, "section": "4.1.2 Exclusion Criteria", "score": 0.93108755, "scores": null, "had_context": true}, {"title": "Protocol Ulcerative Colitis", "page": 11, "section": "Exclusion Criteria", "score": null, "scores": [0.9302051, 0.90958625, 0.8992984], "had_context": true}, {"title": "Protocol Ulcerative Colitis", "page": 12, "section": "Exclusion Criteria", "score": 0.91259205, "scores": null, "had_context": true}], "context_char_count": 6892, "response": "Source: Protocol Ulcerative Colitis.pdf\n\nThe following are all exclusion criteria for the TJ301 ulcerative colitis clinical trial. A subject will not be eligible for inclusion if any of the following criteria apply:\n\n1. Pregnant or breastfeeding women.\n[Section 4.1.2 Exclusion Criteria \u00b7 p.34]\n\n2. Contraindication to colonoscopy or sigmoidoscopy.\n[Section 4.1.2 Exclusion Criteria \u00b7 p.34]\n\n3. Allergies to any component of TJ301.\n[Section 4.1.2 Exclusion Criteria \u00b7 p.34]\n\n4. History of colostomy, colectomy or partial colectomy.\n[Section 4.1.2 Exclusion Criteria \u00b7 p.34]\n\n5. Current diagnosis of inflammatory bowel disease unclassified, Crohn's disease, ischemic colitis, fulminant colitis and/or toxic megacolon, patients with ulcerative colitis limited to the rectum (ulcerative proctitis), infective enteritis, amebic bowel disease and intestinal schistosomiasis.\n[Section 4.1.2 Exclusion Criteria \u00b7 p.34]\n\n6. History of malignancy other than a successfully treated non-metastatic cutaneous squamous cell or basal cell carcinoma and/or localized carcinoma in situ of the cervix. If the Screening colonoscopy shows evidence of dysplasia or a malignancy, the patient is not eligible.\n[Section Exclusion Criteria \u00b7 p.10]\n\n7. Primary or secondary immunodeficiency including neutropenia (absolute neutrophil count <1500/\u03bcL); or lymphopenia (absolute lymphocyte count <500/\u03bcL).\n[Section Exclusion Criteria \u00b7 p.11]\n\n8. Moderate to severe anaemia (haemoglobin <9 g/dL), or thrombocytopenia (platelet count <75,000/\u03bcL), or serum creatinine >2 mg/dL.\n[Section Exclusion Criteria \u00b7 p.11]\n\n9. Autoimmune disease besides UC, with the exceptions of Sjogren's syndrome or hypothyroidism.\n[Section Exclusion Criteria \u00b7 p.11]\n\n10. Clostridium (C.) difficile positive at screening visit or treated for C. difficile within the 4 weeks prior to Randomization.\n[Section Exclusion Criteria \u00b7 p.11]\n\n11. Known clinically relevant chronic liver disease. Impaired hepatic function in the absence of a diagnosis of primary sclerosing cholangitis (serum transaminases >2.5 x ULN, alkaline phosphatase >2.5 x ULN, or abnormalities in synthetic liver function tests judged by the investigator to be clinically significant), or a diagnosis of primary sclerosing cholangitis, serum transaminases >3 x ULN, alkaline phosphatase >3 x ULN, or abnormalities in synthetic liver function tests (total bilirubin >1.5 x ULN) judged by the investigator to be clinically significant.\n[Section Exclusion Criteria \u00b7 p.11]\n\n12. Serious underlying disease other than UC in the opinion of the investigator.\n[Section Exclusion Criteria \u00b7 p.11]\n\n13. History of drug addiction within the last 1 year or current drug addiction or use of illicit drugs.\n[Section Exclusion Criteria \u00b7 p.11]\n\n14. Any indication of the regular use of more than 40 grams of alcohol every day.\n[Section Exclusion Criteria \u00b7 p.11]\n\n15. Smokers who smoke more than 10 cigarettes per day.\n[Section Exclusion Criteria \u00b7 p.11]\n\n16. Known concurrent acute or chronic viral ", "sources": [{"name": "Protocol Ulcerative Colitis", "page": 10, "section": "Exclusion Criteria", "exactText": "", "bboxes": [[72.00000000000018, 355.22398291015617, 520.5600000000003, 344.93497521784843]], "relevance": "high"}, {"name": "Protocol Ulcerative Colitis", "page": 34, "section": "4.1.2 Exclusion Criteria", "exactText": "", "bboxes": [[72.0, 251.66398291015628, 520.5600000000001, 241.3749752178486]], "relevance": "high"}, {"name": "Protocol Ulcerative Colitis", "page": 11, "section": "Exclusion Criteria", "exactText": "", "bboxes": [[72.12, 368.7839829101563, 555.84, 313.0149752178486], [93.6, 732.3839829101563, 418.56, 722.0949752178486], [72.12, 602.1839829101563, 555.8400000000003, 500.81497521784854]], "relevance": "high"}, {"name": "Protocol Ulcerative Colitis", "page": 12, "section": "Exclusion Criteria", "exactText": "", "bboxes": [[72.12, 732.3839829101563, 478.2, 722.0949752178486]], "relevance": "high"}], "timing": {"response_cache_hit": false, "semantic_cache_hit": false, "chunks_compressed": true, "condense_ms": 0.0072498805820941925, "query_condensed": false, "embedding_ms": 688.6420417577028, "embedding_cache_hit": false, "retrieval": {"chunk_cache_hit": false, "confidence_filter_applied": true, "confidence_filter_threshold": 0.04, "confidence_filter_bm25_threshold": null, "confidence_filter_input_count": 46, "confidence_filter_kept_count": 46, "confidence_filter_dropped_count": 0, "confidence_filter_kept_scores": [0.6539, 0.6464, 0.6457, 0.6429, 0.6216, 0.619, 0.602, 0.5972, 0.5548, 0.5349, 0.503, 0.503, 0.4895, 0.4682, 0.46, 0.4501, 0.4481, 0.4467, 0.441, 0.4366, 0.4357, 0.4308, 0.4305, 0.4302, 0.4268, 0.4257, 0.4183, 0.4147, 0.4113, 0.4096, 0.4092, 0.4077, 0.4069, 0.4066, 0.4063, 0.4039, 0.4036, 0.4032, 0.4023, 0.4022, 0.4018, 0.4004, 0.3987, 0.398, 0.3964], "confidence_filter_dropped_scores": [], "confidence_filter_bm25_only_scores_normalized": [0.0], "hybrid_search": true, "cache_hit": true, "embedding_ms":