INFO     rag_service.services.generation_service:generation_service.py:427 {"event": "rag_query_trace", "query": "How is CRP used for stratification in this study?", "retrieval_query": null, "system_prompt_version": "440b2406", "retrieved_chunks": [{"title": "Protocol Ulcerative Colitis", "page": 92, "section": "Appendix 4 - Summary of Changes for Version 1.1", "score": 0.5868188, "scores": null, "had_context": true}, {"title": "Protocol Ulcerative Colitis", "page": 36, "section": "4.2.2 Randomisation", "score": 0.0008328334, "scores": null, "had_context": true}, {"title": "Protocol Ulcerative Colitis", "page": 87, "section": "Exploratory Biomarkers:", "score": 0.0006641048, "scores": null, "had_context": true}, {"title": "Protocol Ulcerative Colitis", "page": 45, "section": "Table 1 Time and Events Schedule", "score": 0.0002824081, "scores": null, "had_context": true}, {"title": "Protocol Ulcerative Colitis", "page": 54, "section": "7.1.1 Clinical and Endoscopic Disease Activity (Mayo Score)", "score": 0.00020342697, "scores": null, "had_context": true}, {"title": "Protocol Ulcerative Colitis", "page": 72, "section": "10.3 Use of Patient Reported Outcome Instruments", "score": 0.00018522576, "scores": null, "had_context": true}], "context_char_count": 6202, "response": "Source: Protocol Ulcerative Colitis.pdf\n\nCRP was originally proposed as a stratification factor but was subsequently replaced in Version 1.1 of the protocol:\n\n1. In the original protocol version, randomisation stratification included elevated CRP levels (\u22653 mg/L) as one of the stratification factors, alongside stable conventional treatment history (prior treatment with amino salicylates, corticosteroids, and immunosuppressive drugs).\n[Section Appendix 4 - Summary of Changes for Version 1.1 \u00b7 p.92]\n\n2. In the revised protocol (Version 1.1), CRP was removed as a stratification factor. Randomisation stratification was updated to be based instead on: prior corticosteroids treatment (yes/no) and consent to participate in PK substudy (yes/no). This change was applied across sections 3.1.2, 4.2.2, and 9.6.2, as well as the Synopsis.\n[Section Appendix 4 - Summary of Changes for Version 1.1 \u00b7 p.92]\n\n3. In the final protocol, CRP is retained only as an exploratory biomarker (measured from blood), and is analysed at local sites alongside ESR, neutrophil count, and platelet count \u2014 but it is no longer used for randomisation stratification.\n[Section Exploratory Biomarkers: \u00b7 p.87]\n[Section Table 1 Time and Events Schedule \u00b7 p.45]", "sources": [{"name": "Protocol Ulcerative Colitis", "page": 92, "section": "Appendix 4 - Summary of Changes for Version 1.1", "exactText": "", "bboxes": [[52.59044647216797, 495.76949310302734, 771.7723999023438, 121.96722412109375]], "relevance": "high"}, {"name": "Protocol Ulcerative Colitis", "page": 36, "section": "4.2.2 Randomisation", "exactText": "", "bboxes": [[72.0, 233.90398291015606, 538.44, 178.01497521784836]], "relevance": "high"}, {"name": "Protocol Ulcerative Colitis", "page": 87, "section": "Exploratory Biomarkers:", "exactText": "", "bboxes": [[72.0, 721.4399829101562, 554.5199999999999, 693.5349752178486]], "relevance": "high"}, {"name": "Protocol Ulcerative Colitis", "page": 45, "section": "Table 1 Time and Events Schedule", "exactText": "", "bboxes": [[77.15952000000003, 132.16128732421873, 795.356639999999, 115.30609217037261]], "relevance": "high"}, {"name": "Protocol Ulcerative Colitis", "page": 54, "section": "7.1.1 Clinical and Endoscopic Disease Activity (Mayo Score)", "exactText": "", "bboxes": [[72.0, 258.9839829101563, 548.76, 187.9749752178485]], "relevance": "high"}, {"name": "Protocol Ulcerative Colitis", "page": 72, "section": "10.3 Use of Patient Reported Outcome Instruments", "exactText": "", "bboxes": [[71.99999999999994, 721.7039829101564, 546.48, 635.5749752178486]], "relevance": "high"}], "timing": {"response_cache_hit": false, "semantic_cache_hit": false, "chunks_