ing the safety and efficacy of TJ301, further confirming it is still in clinical trial stages.\n[Section A Phase II, Randomized, Double-blind, Placebo-controlled Study to Evaluate the Safety and Efficacy of TJ301 (FE 999301) Administered Intravenously in Patients with Active Ulcerative Colitis \u00b7 p.1]\n\nI don't have this information regarding any FDA approval or approval decision for TJ301.", "sources": [{"name": "Protocol Ulcerative Colitis", "page": 22, "section": "1.1 Background", "exactText": "TJ301 (FE 999301, Olamkicept (proposed INN)) is a first-in-class, selective IL-6 trans-signalling inhibitor and anti-inflammatory biologic that is under development for the treatment of UC and Crohn's disease.", "bboxes": [[72.00000000000006, 229.82398291015625, 551.3999999999997, 174.05497521784855]], "relevance": "high"}, {"name": "Protocol Ulcerative Colitis", "page": 1, "section": "A Phase II, Randomized, Double-blind, Placebo-controlled Study to Evaluate the Safety and Efficacy of TJ301 (FE 999301) Administered Intravenously in Patients with Active Ulcerative Colitis", "exactText": "A Phase II, Randomized, Double-blind, Placebo-controlled Study to Evaluate the Safety and Efficacy of TJ301 (FE 999301) Administered Intravenously in Patients with Active Ulcerative Colitis", "bboxes": [[72.0, 578.6639829101563, 168.0, 568.2525283647018]], "relevance": "medium"}], "timing": {"response_cache_hit": false, "semantic_cache_hit": false, "chunks_compressed": false, "condense_ms": 0.0009578652679920197, "query_condensed": false, "embedding_ms": 656.6461669281125, "embedding_cache_hit": false, "retrieval": {"chunk_cache_hit": false, "confidence_filter_applied": true, "confidence_filter_threshold": 0.04, "confidence_filter_bm25_threshold": null, "confidence_filter_input_count": 43, "confidence_filter_kept_count": 43, "confidence_filter_dropped_count": 0, "confidence_filter_kept_scores": [0.5741, 0.5437, 0.6201, 0.5921, 0.5825, 0.5797, 0.5746, 0.5674, 0.5551, 0.5492, 0.5471, 0.