INFO     rag_service.services.generation_service:generation_service.py:427 {"event": "rag_query_trace", "query": "Tell me about CRP.", "retrieval_query": null, "system_prompt_version": "440b2406", "retrieved_chunks": [{"title": "Protocol Ulcerative Colitis", "page": 87, "section": "Exploratory Biomarkers:", "score": 0.032405518, "scores": null, "had_context": true}, {"title": "Protocol Ulcerative Colitis", "page": 7, "section": "Exploratory Endpoints", "score": 0.0065388246, "scores": null, "had_context": true}, {"title": "Protocol Ulcerative Colitis", "page": 45, "section": "Table 1 Time and Events Schedule", "score": 0.002396731, "scores": null, "had_context": true}, {"title": "Protocol Ulcerative Colitis", "page": 71, "section": "10.2 Electronic Case Record Form", "score": null, "scores": [0.0019418169, 0.0011879054], "had_context": true}, {"title": "Protocol Ulcerative Colitis", "page": 18, "section": "List of Abbreviations", "score": 0.0013250224, "scores": null, "had_context": true}], "context_char_count": 5550, "response": "Source: Protocol Ulcerative Colitis.pdf\n\nC-reactive protein (CRP) is referenced in several contexts throughout the protocol:\n\n1. **Definition/Abbreviation:** CRP stands for C-Reactive Protein.\n[Section List of Abbreviations \u00b7 p.18]\n\n2. **Exploratory Biomarker:** CRP is included as an exploratory biomarker measured from blood samples, alongside ESR, IL-6, IL-6/sIL-6R complex, neutrophil and platelet count, and faecal calprotectin.\n[Section Exploratory Biomarkers: \u00b7 p.87]\n\n3. **Exploratory Endpoint:** Change from Baseline to Weeks 4, 8, and 12 in CRP is tracked as part of the exploratory endpoints of the study.\n[Section Exploratory Endpoints \u00b7 p.7]\n\n4. **Analysis Location:** CRP tests are analysed at local sites (not the central laboratory). Additionally, at Visits 2 and 8, patients must be in a fasting state (\u22658 hours) when biomarker samples are collected.\n[Section Table 1 Time and Events Schedule \u00b7 p.