INFO     rag_service.services.generation_service:generation_service.py:427 {"event": "rag_query_trace", "query": "(1) What is the primary endpoint?", "retrieval_query": null, "system_prompt_version": "440b2406", "retrieved_chunks": [{"title": "Protocol Ulcerative Colitis", "page": 68, "section": "9.6.2 Primary Endpoint", "score": null, "scores": [0.9928231, 0.9928231], "had_context": true}, {"title": "Protocol Ulcerative Colitis", "page": 24, "section": "Primary Endpoints", "score": null, "scores": [0.99273914, 0.99273914], "had_context": true}, {"title": "Protocol Ulcerative Colitis", "page": 7, "section": "Primary Endpoints", "score": 0.99273914, "scores": null, "had_context": true}, {"title": "Protocol Ulcerative Colitis", "page": 30, "section": "3.4.2 Selection of Endpoints", "score": 0.9730365, "scores": null, "had_context": true}], "context_char_count": 5106, "response": "Source: Protocol Ulcerative Colitis.pdf\n\nThe primary endpoint of the trial encompasses both an efficacy measure and safety assessments:\n\n1. **Efficacy:** Clinical and endoscopic remission at Week 12, defined as a full Mayo score \u22642, no individual subscore >1, and rectal bleeding subscore = 0.\n[Section Primary Endpoints \u00b7 p.7]\n\n2. **Safety:** Adverse events, vital signs, 12-lead Electrocardiography (ECG), and clinical safety laboratory abnormalities.\n[Section Primary Endpoints \u00b7 p.7]\n\n**Additional context on the efficacy endpoint:**\n\n3. The full Mayo score (range 0\u201312; higher score is worse) is based on the clinician's scoring of clinical signs and symptoms, as well as endoscopic scoring of gross colonic mucosal inflammation. The Mayo score has been extensively used in earlier clinical trials in UC and shows good correlation between the full Mayo score and the clinician-rated components only (partial Mayo score without endoscopy).\n[Section 3.4.2 Selection of Endpoints \u00b7 p.30]\n\n4. For the statistical analysis, this binary outcome (remission status = yes/no) will be analysed by a logistic regression model with treatment and the randomisation-stratification factors (prior corticosteroids treatment and consent to participate in PK substudy) as fixed effects and the baseline full Mayo score as covariate. A patient with missing data on the remission status will be assumed to be not in remission.\n[Section 9.6.2 Primary Endpoint \u00b7 p.68]", "sources": [{"name": "Protocol Ulcerative Colitis", "page": 68, "section": "9.6.2 Primary Endpoint", "exactText": "", "bboxes": [[71.99999999999997, 721.7039829101564, 558.8399999999996, 605.2149752178486], [71.99999999999997, 721.7039829101564, 558.8399999999996, 605.2149752178486]], "relevance": "high"}, {"name": "Protocol Ulcerative Colitis", "page": 24, "section": "Primary Endpoints", "exactText": "", "bboxes": [[89.88000000000005, 432.8399829101563, 509.16, 406.8549752178486], [89.88000000000005, 432.8399829101563, 509.16, 406.8549752178486]], "relevance": "high"}, {"name": "Protocol Ulcerative Colitis", "page": 7, "section": "Primary Endpoints", "exactText": "", "bboxes": [[90.0, 646.0799829101562, 514.9199999999998, 619.2549752178485]], "relevance": "high"}, {"name": "Protocol Ulcerative Colitis", "page": 30, "section": "3.4.2 Selection of Endpoints", "exactText": "", "bboxes": [[71.99999999999994, 664.2239829101562, 549.4800000000001, 517.3749752178485]], "relevance": "high"}], "timing": {"response_cache_hit": false, "semantic_cache_hit": false, "chunks_compressed": true, "condense_ms": 0.0040424056351184845, "query_condensed": false, "embedding_ms": 715.5184578150511, "embedding_cache_hit": false, "retrieval": {"chunk_cache_hit": false, "confidence_filter_applied": true, "confidence_filter_threshold": 0.04, "confidence_filter_bm25_threshold": null, "confidence_filter_input_count": 48, "confidence_filter_kept_count": 48, "confidence_filter_dropped_count": 0, "confidence_filter_kept_scores": [0.5652, 0.5262, 0.5692, 0.5662, 0.5605, 0.5556, 0.5414, 0.5296, 0.5176, 0.511, 0.509