INFO     rag_service.services.generation_service:generation_service.py:427 {"event": "rag_query_trace", "query": "(1) How is the drug dosed?", "retrieval_query": null, "system_prompt_version": "440b2406", "retrieved_chunks": [{"title": "Protocol Ulcerative Colitis", "page": 31, "section": "3.4.4 Selection of Doses in the Trial", "score": 0.19744445, "scores": null, "had_context": true}, {"title": "Protocol Ulcerative Colitis", "page": 30, "section": "3.4.4 Selection of Doses in the Trial", "score": null, "scores": [0.058776557, 0.058776557], "had_context": true}, {"title": "Protocol Ulcerative Colitis", "page": 39, "section": "5.1 Treatments Administered", "score": null, "scores": [0.041930523, 0.027376488], "had_context": true}, {"title": "Protocol Ulcerative Colitis", "page": 32, "section": "3.4.4 Selection of Doses in the Trial", "score": 0.016529556, "scores": null, "had_context": true}], "context_char_count": 6818, "response": "Source: Protocol Ulcerative Colitis.pdf\n\nThe dosing of TJ301 is described across several aspects \u2014 dose levels, formulation, and administration:\n\n1. **Dose levels:** Two doses are investigated in the trial \u2014 300 mg and 600 mg \u2014 both selected to achieve exposure above the full target saturation threshold of 1 \u00b5g/mL at trough.\n[Section 3.4.4 Selection of Doses in the Trial \u00b7 p.32]\n\n2. **Route and formulation:** TJ301 is administered as an intravenous (i.v.) infusion, formulated at 15 mg/mL in 5 mL vials, and diluted in 250 mL of 5% (w/v) glucose for infusion (resulting in 1.03 mg/mL for the 300 mg group and 2.07 mg/mL for the 600 mg group). The placebo group receives 0 mg/mL TJ301 in the same vehicle.\n[Section 5.1 Treatments Administered \u00b7 p.39]\n\n3. **Infusion duration:** The infusion time is 2 hours.\n[Section 5.1 Treatments Administered \u00b7 p.39]\n\n4. **Dose frequency:** The doses and dose frequency were selected to be within the safe and tolerable range established in Phase 1, while aiming to limit the number of i.v. infusion events. The exact dosing interval (e.g., weekly, every 4 weeks) is not specified in the provided context. I don't have this information regarding the precise dosing schedule/frequency.\n[Section 3.4.4 Selection of Doses in the Trial \u00b7 p.30]\n\n5. **Pharmacokinetic basis:** Phase 1 data showed dose proportionality in Cmax and AUC, with a terminal half-life of approximately 4.7 days, supporting the selected dose levels.\n[Section 3.4.4 Selection of Doses in the Trial \u00b7 p.30]", "sources": [{"name": "Protocol Ulcerative Colitis", "page": 32, "section": "3.4.4 Selection of Doses in the Trial", "exactText": "The two doses selected are within the range of doses investigated in phase 1 with dose proportionality in systemic exposure, and with no evident safety signals. The two doses are selected to give exposure above (300 and 600 mg) full target saturation (expected at the theoretical threshold of 1 \u00b5g/mL at trough).", "bboxes": [[71.99999999999994, 422.7839829101563, 552.8399999999997, 336.6549752178485]], "relevance": "high"}, {"name": "Protocol Ulcerative Colitis", "page": 39, "section": "5.1 Treatments Administered", "exactText": "Both placebo and TJ301 should be stored at -20 \u00b1 5\u00b0C and thawed at the site by site personnel (blind to study randomisation) and diluted in 250 mL 5% (w/v) glucose (1.03 mg/mL TJ301 for the 300 mg group, 2.07 mg/mL TJ301 for the 600 mg group and 0 mg/mL TJ301 for the placebo group). The infusion time is 2 hours.", "bboxes": [[71.99999999999997, 689.9039829101564, 523.8, 664.4949752178487], [71.99999999999994, 459.52798291015654, 201.59999999999994, 448.9749752178488]], "relevance": "high"}, {"name": "Protocol Ulcerative Colitis", "page": 30, "section": "3.4.4 Selection of Doses in the Trial", "exactText": "Pharmacokinetic results indicate dose proportionality in maximal concentration obtained (Cmax) and overall exposure (AUC) with a terminal half-life of approximately 4.7 days. The doses and dose frequency selected for this trial are within a dose range that is considered safe and tolerable in healthy subjects and patients, trying to limit the number of i.v. infusion events.", "bboxes": [[72.00000000000006, 263.9039829101562, 543.4800000000001, 192.89497521784858]], "relevance": "high"}, {"name": "Protocol Ulcerative Colitis", "page": 31, "section": "3.4.4 Selection of Doses in the Trial", "exactText": "target saturation resulting in a suppression of STAT-3 activation back to baseline levels is expected to occur above an exposure of 1 \u00b5g/mL. Thus, the dose levels for this trial were selected to test levels of exposure around the threshold.", "bboxes": [[71.99999999999966, 502.10398291015616, 544.4399999999995, 415.8549752178484]], "relevance": "medium"}], "timing": {"response_cache_hit": false, "semantic_cache_hit": false, "chunks_compressed": true, "condense_ms": 0.0009583309292793274, "query_condensed": false, "embedding_ms": 747.3089592531323, "embedding_cache_hit": false, "retrieval": {"chunk_cache_hit": false, "confidence_filter_applied": true, "confidence_filter_threshold": 0.04, "confidence_filter_bm25_threshold": null, "confidence_filter_input_count": 47, "confidence_filter_kept_count": 47, "confidence_filter_dropped_count": 0, "confidence_filter_kept_scores": [0.4613, 0.4321, 0.4272, 0.4257, 0.4248, 0.4204, 0.4204, 0.4177, 0.4174, 0.4148, 0.413, 0.4117, 0.411, 0.4109, 0.4092, 0.4087, 0.4061, 0.4039, 0.4019, 0.4014, 0.4, 0.3953, 0.3928, 0.3919, 0.3915, 0.3904, 0.388, 0.3875, 0.3853, 0.3851, 0.3839, 0.3829, 0.3819, 0.3807, 0.3807, 0.3805, 0.3796, 0.3787, 0.3782, 0.3724, 0.3721, 0.3712, 0.3712, 0.3694, 0.369], "confidence_filter_dropped_scores": [], "confidence_filter_bm25_only_scores_normalized": [1.0, 0.0], "hybrid_search": true, "cache_hit": true, "embedding_ms": 0.0, "db_search_ms": 5647.181665990502, "hybrid_parallel_ms": 6054.887542035431, "vector_count": 45, "bm25_count": 2, "fused_count": 47, "reranker_enabled": true, "reranker