INFO     rag_service.services.generation_service:generation_service.py:427 {"event": "rag_query_trace", "query": "What fields should the eCRF include based on this protocol?", "retrieval_query": null, "system_prompt_version": "440b2406", "retrieved_chunks": [{"title": "Protocol Ulcerative Colitis", "page": 75, "section": "12.2 Deviations from the Protocol", "score": 0.48947302, "scores": null, "had_context": true}, {"title": "Protocol Ulcerative Colitis", "page": 71, "section": "10.2 Electronic Case Record Form", "score": null, "scores": [0.36692992, 0.022542967], "had_context": true}, {"title": "Protocol Ulcerative Colitis", "page": 63, "section": "8.5.2 Collection, Recording and Reporting of Serious Adverse Events SAE Reporting by the Investigator", "score": null, "scores": [0.09073549, 0.053899154], "had_context": true}, {"title": "Protocol Ulcerative Colitis", "page": 58, "section": "8.2.2 Recording of Adverse Events", "score": 0.026056303, "scores": null, "had_context": true}], "context_char_count": 6908, "response": "Source: Protocol Ulcerative Colitis.pdf\n\nBased on the protocol, the e-CRF must include the following fields and components:\n\n**1. Adverse Event Log fields (per Section 8.2.2):**\nEach adverse event must be recorded with the following information:\n- Adverse event\n- Date of onset (time can be recorded, if applicable)\n- Intensity\n- Causal relationship to IMP\n- Action taken to IMP\n- Other action taken\n- Date and time of outcome\n- Outcome\n- Seriousness\n[Section 8.2.2 Recording of Adverse Events \u00b7 p.58]\n\n**2. Mandatory logs for SAE reporting (per Section 8.5.2):**\nThe following logs are mandatory for initial SAE reports and for follow-up reports if any relevant changes have been made:\n- Demographics\n- Adverse Event Log\n- Medical History Log\n- Concomitant Medication Log\n[Section 8.5.2 Collection, Recording and Reporting of Serious Adverse Events SAE Reporting by the Investigator \u00b7 p.63]\n\n**3. SAE Report Form:**\nThe SAE Report Form must be included within the e-CRF system and completed and submitted according to the instructions provided on the form.\n[Section 8.5.2 Collection, Recording and Reporting of Serious Adverse Events SAE Reporting by the Investigator \u00b7 p.63]\n\n**4. Protocol Deviation documentation:**\nAny protocol deviation must be documented (or included in e-CRF data), accompanied by a description of the deviation, the relevant dates (start and stop), and the action taken.\n[Section 12.2 Deviations from the Protocol \u00b7 p.75]\n\n**5. Audit trail functionality:**\nErrors in the e-CRF must be corrected electronically, with corrections/modifications automatically tracked by an audit trail detailing the date and time of the correction and the name of the person making the correction.\n[Section 10.2 Electronic Case Record Form \u00b7 p.71]", "sources": [{"name": "Protocol Ulcerative Colitis", "page": 75, "section": "12.2 Deviations from the Protocol", "exactText": "", "bboxes": [[71.99999999999994, 515.6639829101564, 554.28, 429.5349752178486]], "relevance": "high"}, {"name": "Protocol Ulcerative Colitis", "page": 71, "section": "10.2 Electronic Case Record Form", "exactText": "", "bboxes": [[72.00000000000006, 428.42398291015644, 554.4000000000001, 387.7749752178487], [71.99999999999994, 183.1439829101563, 551.0399999999998, 142.4949752178486]], "relevance": "high"}, {"name": "Protocol Ulcerative Colitis", "page": 63, "section": "8.5.2 Collection, Recording and Reporting of Serious Adverse Events SAE Reporting by the Investigator", "exactText": "", "bboxes": [[72.00000000000011, 135.8639829101562, 541.0800000000002, 110.45497521784853], [72.0, 369.2639829101563, 555.6, 267.89497521784847]], "relevance": "high"}, {"name": "Protocol Ulcerative Colitis", "page": 58, "section": "8.2.2 Recording of Adverse Events", "exactText": "", "bboxes": [[72.00000000000011, 188.78398291015662, 511.32, 163.25497521784894]], "relevance": "high"}], "timing": {"response_cache_hit": fal